-- `T WITHAL` on a rule: the error says a rule is not a record, and for a rule
-- some of whose inputs have no default it points at WITH. (A rule every input of
-- which has a default has its own sentence: not-ok/tc/withal-not-a-record.l4.)

GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

#EVAL scaled WITHAL
